Ok, we can debate that. First you would need to justify the need for
a metaphysics place for jetnu in the first place. Why for jetnu and not
for blanu, mlatu, klama, etc, etc. In other words, what is the difference
between these sentences:

1-            la djan cu xusra le du'u ti mlatu
               John asserts that this is a cat.

2-           la djan cu xusra le du'u le du'u ta mlat cu fatci
               John asserts that it is a fact that this is a cat.

3-            la djan cu xusra le du'u le du'u ta mlatu cu jetnu ko'a
               John asserts that by metaphysics koha
                it is true that this is a cat.

Is (1) closer to (2) or to (3)? From your comments about fatci
I suppose you'd say it is closer to (3). How come then that in
(1) there is no place for the metaphysics koha? Shouldn't xusra
have a place for the metaphysics for which the x1 asserts that
x2 is true?

